# TODO — opm repair sequence (detailed)
File: opm/audit/todo.oot
Date: 2026-09-04. Repo: opm only. Tag at audit: v2.11.1.

Stay in opm/. Do not start a later phase until the current phase
hostile probes fail on old code, then pass twice.

Do not add subcommands. Do not leave this repo. Do not write
CLAUDE.md or extra .md files. Version is the git tag (RFC-0006).
Files of product code stay at or under 256 lines.

Keep (do not rewrite): resolve/, lock/ lock lines, policy/caps,
qa proofs that already assert. The unique move is cap-aware
resolve. The CLI wrapper is what lies.

Rule of work: extract a pure helper the probe can call. Do not
spawn the opm binary in Phase 0. oodac check can fake-pass; a
proof must assert and process_exit(1) on miss.


## Live command surface (truth)

main.oo dispatches these names (this is the product):

  add
  audit, sbom          (sbom currently calls audit, not sbom)
  bot
  ingest
  init
  launch
  remove, update, outdated, why
  pack
  pkg
  publish
  regs, reg, registry  (all three call run_ooda_pm_regs)
  search
  tree, vendor, clean

Help and docs also list these. main.oo does NOT dispatch them:

  cat, git, io, more, pick, ops

Those files are helpers. Help lies. cli/ANCHOR.oo claims
"19 subcommand handlers" and lists the helpers as commands.


## Phase 0 — Probes first (no product fix yet)

Write qa drivers that fail on today's code. Wire each name into
scripts/test.oo. Double-run after they fail (they must fail, not
fake-pass).

### P0.1 qa/argv_init_proof.oo

Today: run_ooda_pm_init starts `i = 2`. main.oo already sliced
argv to rest, so `opm init myapp` arrives as rest=["myapp"].
The loop never sees myapp. Name becomes "pkg".

Extract (or add, then probe against today's loop) a helper:

  pm_init_name(args: List[String]) -> String

Probe cases (must fail today):

  pm_init_name(["myapp"])            == "myapp"     FAIL today -> "pkg"
  pm_init_name(["--json", "myapp"])  == "myapp"
  pm_init_name(["myapp", "--json"])  == "myapp"
  pm_init_name([])                   == "pkg"       default only when empty
  pm_init_name(["--json"])           == "pkg"
  pm_name_ok("../x") is false; init must refuse that name

qa/init_proof.oo today only checks pm_init_manifest in memory.
It does not cover argv. Keep it. P0.1 is the argv proof.

### P0.2 qa/argv_bot_proof.oo and qa/argv_publish_proof.oo

Today: cmd_bot.oo parse starts `i = 1`. rest=["registry"] is
skipped. Target stays the default "registry" by luck when the
user passes that word, and skips any other first positional.

Today: cmd_publish.oo parse starts `i = 1`. rest=["--to",
"/tmp/r"] skips "--to". Publish writes to
`.ooda-cache/registry` instead of `/tmp/r`.

Helpers to extract:

  pm_bot_target(args) -> String     default "registry"
  pm_publish_to(args) -> String     default ".ooda-cache/registry"
  pm_publish_json(args) -> Bool

Probe cases (must fail today):

  pm_bot_target(["mydir"])                 == "mydir"
  pm_bot_target(["--sign", "mydir"])       == "mydir"
  pm_bot_target(["mydir", "--sign"])       == "mydir"
  pm_publish_to(["--to", "/tmp/r"])        == "/tmp/r"
  pm_publish_json(["--json"])              == true
  pm_publish_to([])                        == ".ooda-cache/registry"

### P0.3 qa/help_surface_proof.oo

Extract print_help body to a String function:

  pm_help_text() -> String

Canonical live names (one list in the proof):

  add audit sbom bot ingest init launch
  remove update outdated why
  pack pkg publish
  reg registry regs
  search tree vendor clean

Must appear. Must NOT appear as subcommands:

  cat git io more pick ops

Also refuse the phrase "19 subcommand" in cli/ANCHOR.oo and
docs/cli.oot once Phase 2 rewrites them. For Phase 0, only
assert against pm_help_text() / print_help.

Today print_help lists cat, git, io, more, pick. Probe fails.

### P0.4 qa/compiler_token_proof.oo

Today find_oodac (cli/find_compiler.oo) order:

  1. OODA_COMPILER
  2. bin/oodac            FALLBACK — kill
  3. ooda/oodac_bin       FALLBACK — kill
  then process_exit(1)

Extract a Result helper (do not process_exit in the helper):

  resolve_oodac(fs, env) -> Result[String, String]

Phase 0 may start as a source probe if EnvCap is hard to mock:

  slurp cli/find_compiler.oo
  FAIL if the file contains `bin/oodac`
  FAIL if the file contains `ooda/oodac_bin`
  FAIL if scripts/build.oo, scripts/test.oo, scripts/release.oo
       contain a second copy of find_oodac after Phase 3
       (Phase 0 only flags cli/find_compiler.oo fallbacks)

scripts/ already refuse unset OODA_COMPILER. The lie is only
in cli/find_compiler.oo.

### P0.5 qa/no_shell_proof.oo

Source probe. Walk these files (exact list):

  cli/host_run.oo
  cli/cmd_git.oo
  cli/cmd_reg.oo
  cli/cmd_bot.oo
  registry/regs.oo

FAIL if the text contains: sys_exec(proc, "sh"
FAIL if the text contains: "sh", "-c"
FAIL if the text contains: command -v

Today all five fail. After Phase 3, host_run.oo must pass.
After Phase 4, the rest must pass.

Do not "fix" the probe by deleting the grep. The product
files must lose the shell.

### P0.6 qa/sbom_dispatch_proof.oo

Today: main.oo `sub == "audit" || sub == "sbom"` both call
run_ooda_pm_audit. run_ooda_pm_sbom exists in cmd_audit.oo
and is never reached from main.

Extract a tiny dispatch table test, or assert in a helper:

  pm_dispatch_handler("sbom") == "sbom"
  pm_dispatch_handler("audit") == "audit"

Today both would be "audit". Probe fails. Fix is T2.2.

### P0.7 Wire into scripts/test.oo

Today the driver list is 8 names. Add the new proofs to that
list. Do not remove the 8. Still oodac check until T6.1.

Double-run. Confirm each new proof FAILs on current main.


## Phase 1 — Argv rest contract

main.oo already passes rest. Handlers must read from index 0.
Prefer pm_arg_name(args) / pm_flag / pm_opt from cmd_io.oo.
Do not skip by magic index.

### T1.1 cli/cmd_init.oo

Delete `let mut i: Int = 2`.
Use pm_init_name(args) from P0.1.
Default name "pkg" only when rest has no positional.
Comments say SysCap; signature is ProcessCap. Fix comments
in this pass or in T5.4 — do not leave SysCap in the header.

### T1.2 cli/cmd_bot.oo

Delete `let mut i: Int = 1`.
Use pm_bot_target(args). Skip only flags (`--sign`), never
the first positional.

### T1.3 cli/cmd_publish.oo

Delete `let mut i: Int = 1` in run_ooda_pm_publish.
The mkdir_p loop that walks path chars (also `i = 1`) is a
different i — leave that one.
Use pm_publish_to / pm_publish_json.

### T1.4 cli/cmd_io.oo pm_is_verb

Today the verb skip-list is incomplete. Missing at least:
init, bot, publish, pack is present, ingest is present,
reg, regs, search is present, launch is present.
Add every live dispatch name so a user who accidentally
passes a full argv still does not treat the verb as a
package name. After Phase 1, rest should not contain the
verb, so this is belt-and-braces.

Also add init/bot/publish to the skip list now, because
pm_arg_name is the shared helper.

### T1.5 Audit remaining cli/cmd_*.oo

Grep for `i: Int = 1` and `i: Int = 2` in cli/.
Known remaining after T1.1–T1.3: none in cmd_* handlers
except path-walk loops (publish mkdir_p, string scans).
Those are not argv. Leave them.

cmd_add, cmd_launch, cmd_ops, cmd_pack, cmd_ingest,
cmd_tree already use pm_arg_name. Confirm. Do not "fix"
string-scan loops.

### T1.6 Re-run P0.1 and P0.2. Both must pass twice.


