## Phase 3 — Compiler spawn, no copies, no shell in host_run

opm is not ooda build. Do not keep a fork of ooda/build.

### T3.1 cli/find_compiler.oo

OODA_COMPILER only. Delete:

  take_compiler(fs, "bin/oodac")
  take_compiler(fs, "ooda/oodac_bin")

Unset or missing file is Err. No PATH. No HOME.
find_src_root uses OODA_HOME then OODA_SRC_ROOT. After T3.2,
grep who calls find_src_root. If nobody, delete it.

Return Result[String, String] from resolve_oodac. Callers
print ERR and exit. Do not process_exit inside the helper
(proofs cannot catch that).

### T3.2 cli/host_run.oo

Delete sq() if nothing else in this file needs it.
(cmd_git, cmd_reg, cmd_bot import host_run for sq. After
Phase 4 they must not. If they still import sq in Phase 3,
move sq to a tiny quote helper or delete with them.)

Replace:

  sys_exec(proc, "sh", "-c", cmd)

with argv exec:

  sys_exec(proc, oodac, arg0, arg1, ...)

run_oodac_check already does this for the check path. Make
run_oodac do the same. Kill the string join.

Delete run_ooda_eval and run_ooda_repl. No main.oo branch
calls them. Grep after delete.

refuse_cli that runs `path --version` and checks the first
token is "oodac" can stay if launch still needs it. It must
use sys_exec(proc, path, "--version"), not sh.

### T3.3 cli/host_build.oo

This is an ooda-build clone (target, LTO, sanitizers, PGO).
cmd_launch.oo imports it.

Read run_ooda_pm_launch --exec path. If it only needs
`oodac run <file>`, delete host_build.oo and call host_run
/ sys_exec(proc, oodac, "run", file) from launch.

If launch needs a flag or two, write a tiny
cli/launch_exec.oo (< 80 lines). Do not keep PGO/LTO/wasm
flags inside a package manager.

### T3.4 cli/cmd_launch.oo

Require EnvCap + OODA_COMPILER for --exec. No PATH.
OODA_UNTRUSTED already refuses exec. Keep that.
Missing compiler is Err, not a hunt.

### T3.5 One find_oodac

Today copies live in:

  cli/find_compiler.oo     (has fallbacks — the bug)
  scripts/build.oo         (already OODA_COMPILER only)
  scripts/test.oo          (already OODA_COMPILER only)
  scripts/release.oo       (already OODA_COMPILER only)

Product code (cli/) uses find_compiler.oo.
Scripts may keep a local 15-line copy so a script does not
import cli/. That is allowed if the copy has no fallbacks
and matches the contract. Do not invent a fourth copy.

### T3.6 P0.4 must pass. P0.5 must pass for host_run.oo.

host_run.oo must contain zero `sh -c`. cmd_git / cmd_reg /
cmd_bot / registry/regs.oo still fail P0.5 until Phase 4.
That is expected. Split the probe per-file or keep a
known-fail list in the proof with a phase comment — better:
P0.5 lists files; after T3.2, remove host_run.oo from the
