## Phase 4 — Network and git fail-closed

ProcessCap is not a NetCap. PATH is not a minisign token.
$HOME is not a registry root.

### T4.1 cli/cmd_git.oo  (pm_git_clone_head)

Today one sh -c does: rm -rf dest; git clone; checkout;
rev-parse HEAD. exit 0 always, so git failure becomes
"err git" only after a HEAD mismatch.

Replace with argv execs, each checked:

  sys_exec(proc, git, "clone", "--", url, dest)
  sys_exec(proc, git, "-C", dest, "checkout", commit)
  sys_exec(proc, git, "-C", dest, "rev-parse", "HEAD")

Git binary: do not PATH-hunt. Either

  require env OODA_GIT (like OODA_COMPILER), or
  refuse with err git until a ProcessCap git helper exists.

Allow-list (pm_url_allowed) stays. First. No clone if the
url is not allowed.

Do not keep `exit 0` at the end of a shell string.

### T4.2 cli/cmd_reg.oo

pm_reg_minisign_ok: delete `command -v minisign`. Missing
binary is Err, not echo 127. Require OODA_MINISIGN or a
fixed spawn path under OODACODEX. No PATH.

pm_reg_pull: delete `curl` via sh -c. Options:

  A. Refuse network in this repo until a NetCap fetch
     primitive exists. File vendor / --from only.
  B. sys_exec(proc, curl_path, "-fsS", "--max-time", "30",
     "-o", dest, "--", url) with curl_path from env
     OODA_CURL, and the function takes an explicit token
     in the signature so HTTPS is not ambient.

Prefer A if B needs a new cap type that oodac does not
have. Do not fake NetCap with ProcessCap.

mkdir: use fs_mkdir_p / pm_mkdir, not `mkdir -p` in sh.

### T4.3 registry/regs.oo  pm_regs_home

Today: sh -c `printf %s "$HOME/.config/ooda"`.
That is ambient HOME plus shell.

Replace: EnvCap env_get "OODA_CONFIG" or "XDG_CONFIG_HOME"
only if the function already receives EnvCap. Today it
does not — it takes FsReadCap + ProcessCap. Fail closed:

  extras file under the project (e.g. .ooda-cache/registries)
  or require EnvCap and OODA_CONFIG.

Do not read $HOME. Stock registry URL may stay first.

### T4.4 cli/cmd_bot.oo

Delete sh -c that writes catalog with printf/cp.
Use write_file / pm_place.

Delete sh -c minisign sign. Same rule as T4.2: missing
minisign is Err when --sign is set; without --sign, do
not sign. Do not `|| true`.

Hardcoded package list hello/mid/world/evilcap/tooyank:
bot currently warns and continues on a failed package.
Fail closed: first failed verify is Err, or skip only
packages that are absent (not packages that fail sha).
Do this in the same pass. A warning path is a fallback.

### T4.5 HTTPS and caps

main.oo takes FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. HTTPS fetch
must either:

  disappear (file vendor only), or
  take a real network token in the handler signature.

Do not add a NetCap type in this repo if oodac does not
export one. Ask before inventing a cap.

cmd_reg Setup comment says SysCap. Lie. Fix the comment
when the function changes.

### T4.6 cli/cmd_pick.oo  (vendor_pick.oo after T2.4)

Delete:

  if path_exists(fr, "../registry") { return "../registry"; }

Bare add: --vendor, --from, or a listed store only.
Missing store is Err. No sibling-repo fallback.
That path is a polyrepo leak (opm assuming ../registry).

### T4.7 P0.5 must pass on all five files. Twice.


